WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.426 --> 00:00:04.073
Unit fourteen. Understanding Wi-Fi!

2
00:00:04.984 --> 00:00:09.513
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:12.550
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.525
Today we learn about Understanding Wi-Fi. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:22.518
Wi-Fi. Say it with me. Wi-Fi!

6
00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:30.639
Wireless. Say it with me. Wireless!

7
00:00:34.124 --> 00:00:38.024
Network. Say it with me. Network!

8
00:00:41.526 --> 00:00:45.292
Signal. Say it with me. Signal!

9
00:00:48.798 --> 00:00:52.831
Router. Say it with me. Router!

10
00:00:56.326 --> 00:01:00.059
Connect. Say it with me. Connect!

11
00:01:03.593 --> 00:01:07.759
Password. Say it with me. Password!

12
00:01:11.245 --> 00:01:16.450
Internet access. Say it with me. Internet access!

13
00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:28.801
Wi-Fi is a wireless network that gives me internet access. A router sends a signal, and I connect using a password.

14
00:01:28.851 --> 00:01:32.447
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.733
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:39.933
Network!

17
00:01:40.949 --> 00:01:46.428
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:47.628
Password!

19
00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:57.569
Did you know? The word 'Wi-Fi' doesn't actually stand for anything specific — it was created as a catchy brand name!

20
00:01:57.619 --> 00:02:00.181
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:01.101 --> 00:02:11.710
Think and answer. Why do you think a Wi-Fi network is usually protected with a password?

22
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.990
Great answer!

23
00:02:13.998 --> 00:02:18.893
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:18.943 --> 00:02:22.208
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

